  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...The remnants of Isaias are forecast to round \nthe upper level ridge and move off the Northern Mid-Atlantic \nCoast early next week. Drier air then moves in behind it with \ndrying conditions developing through the upcoming week. With the\ndrier air in place, overnight lows should be seasonably cool, \nbut building hts will lead to above climo high temps in the \nupper 70s to low 80s early in the week, and then even higher \ntemps in the upper 80s to near 90 inland by mid week. Mostly \nsunny skies with high pressure will keep any rain chances away.",
